{"entryId":"2261","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2261:1","sourceSha256":"4efa2149abc2b879b2160bd4609c17fc9b1d67bc2e687cffddde834cb6f217b8","englishSha256":"1ee6b58232c8834196fd670831394fd4de87dd94662d0135e5073b76a387eaff","citations":[{"id":"2261:1:link-01","he":[141,154],"en":[235,245],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.9"},"reference":"Yoma 47a:9","assessment":"The Bavli confirms the four kav and the substitutions by Yeshavav and Yosef. It says Kimḥit had seven sons total and preserves the sages’ reservation about her explanation. The English retains Heilprin’s seven-brothers formulation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 47a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 47a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 47a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 47a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Bavli confirms the four kav and the substitutions by Yeshavav and Yosef. It says Kimḥit had seven sons total and preserves the sages’ reservation about her explanation. The English retains Heilprin’s seven-brothers formulation.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Preserve the contrast between Heilprin’s seven brothers and the Bavli’s seven sons, and attribute the explanation about her hair to the narrative.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 47a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 47a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_47a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic